FINDING 9: docs/WORKFLOW_DESIGN_METHOD.md:210 | low | "Depends on" is defined by whether one answer "might" remove or change another spot. Almost any two spots meet that test, so the field cannot be checked and does not reliably order the questions. | QUOTE: | Depends on | another spot whose answer might remove or change this one |
VERDICT: Step 3 is unsound on the order of its parts. The diagram resolves every spot before sizing, while the method holds pieces back until the design is answered and the dotted edge starts them early, so the three artifacts disagree. On top of that, nothing defines information versus unknown, nothing checks the list is complete, and a newly found spot has no route back into the list.
